      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the list. i'll start with the cross-referencing. one thing though, the discrepancies are really small—like, way under the threshold for any major red flag. it's almost like they're just... slipping through the cracks. i'm worried that by the time we get enough data to prove a pattern, the amounts will have added up to something significant. is there a way to specifically target these \"tiny\" gaps? maybe a way to look for things that are purposely staying small enough to go unnoticed?",
